meta {
  name: 10 View my own public profile (what owners see)
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/users/{{emeka_id}}/profile
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.id: isDefined
  res.body.role: eq AGENT
  res.body.fullName: isDefined
  res.body.suspended: eq false
  res.body.reviewCount: isDefined
  res.body.averageRating: isDefined
}

docs {
  This is THE screen. This is what an owner like Biodun sees when he's
  deciding between me and the agency down the road. Every trust signal that's
  here is one less call I have to make to prove myself; every signal that's
  missing is a deal I lose.

  What I'm checking (persona doc Story 9 says these were "Future"):
  - `closedDealCount` — do owners see how many deals I've actually closed?
  - `responseRate` — do they see I reply within an hour?

  Post-audit hinted these would be added. The PublicUserProfile schema in
  the spec currently lists: id, fullName, displayName, role,
  identityVerifiedAt, agentCredentialVerifiedAt, suspended, averageRating,
  reviewCount, joinedAt — and that's it. So this is more of a "did they
  actually ship it?" reality check.

  My credentials are still PENDING in this run, so I expect
  `agentCredentialVerifiedAt` = null. That's fine. But the *fields existing
  at all* is what matters here.
}
